    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation first creates a dense feature field, then partitions that field into windows without dropping tokens.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder turns the low-resolution image into the dense feature field that carries spatial detail. The window operator then partitions that field into tokens for the thought process. The equation keeps the carrier visible while the camera closes in on the windowed tokens.",
